mactelnet-proxy (0.1.9) stable; urgency=low

  * generalize deployment-specific examples in comments and Docker
    defaults — Dockerfile MACTELNET_PROXY_KEYS_DIR default moved
    from /config/auth (VyOS-flavored) to /etc/mactelnet-proxy so it
    matches the systemd unit and the binary default. Comment
    examples for MACTELNET_PROXY_INTERFACE switched from bond0 /
    bond0.3006 to eth0 / eth1.
  * Debian-package deploys are unaffected — the systemd unit pins
    MACTELNET_PROXY_KEYS_DIR=/etc/mactelnet-proxy explicitly.
    Docker users with a volume mounted at /config/auth need to
    remount on /etc/mactelnet-proxy (or set
    MACTELNET_PROXY_KEYS_DIR=/config/auth back via -e).

 -- Icosa Consulting <build@icosa.consulting>  Fri, 01 May 2026 21:00:00 -0600

mactelnet-proxy (0.1.8) stable; urgency=low

  * default keys dir rebased: /etc/netcfg-mactelnet-proxy →
    /etc/mactelnet-proxy. Matches what postinst has always created
    and what the systemd unit sets via MACTELNET_PROXY_KEYS_DIR, so
    no migration needed for package-installed deployments.
  * default host-key filename renamed: ssh_host_ed25519_key →
    mactel_ed25519_key. Existing installs upgraded in place will
    auto-generate a new key on first start and present a fresh SSH
    host fingerprint to clients — rename the old file to keep the
    existing fingerprint:
      mv /etc/mactelnet-proxy/ssh_host_ed25519_key \
         /etc/mactelnet-proxy/mactel_ed25519_key

 -- Icosa Consulting <build@icosa.consulting>  Fri, 01 May 2026 20:00:00 -0600

mactelnet-proxy (0.1.7) stable; urgency=low

  * service runs as root/root (the systemd default) instead of a
    dedicated mactelnet user — the daemon needs CAP_NET_RAW +
    PF_PACKET anyway, and User=mactelnet was tripping DAC on
    operator-owned key paths (e.g. /config/auth on VyOS) without
    actually shrinking the privilege surface. CapabilityBoundingSet
    + Protect*/Restrict*/SystemCallFilter still meaningfully
    constrain the root daemon.
  * postinst no longer creates the mactelnet user/group; postrm no
    longer deletes them. /etc/mactelnet-proxy is now installed
    root:root 0700.
  * vrf.conf drop-in simplified: no User= override needed, dropped
    AmbientCapabilities (no-op for root). Still expands
    CapabilityBoundingSet, relaxes SystemCallFilter, and sets
    ProtectControlGroups=no for `ip vrf exec`'s cgroup mkdir.

 -- Icosa Consulting <build@icosa.consulting>  Fri, 01 May 2026 19:00:00 -0600

mactelnet-proxy (0.1.6) stable; urgency=low

  * fix(vrf): drop-in now sets ProtectControlGroups=no — without it
    the base unit's ProtectControlGroups=yes makes /sys/fs/cgroup
    read-only, and `ip vrf exec` fails when it tries to mkdir a
    sub-cgroup for its eBPF program ("Failed to setup vrf cgroup2
    directory"). Filed under the same drop-in at
    /usr/share/doc/mactelnet-proxy/examples/vrf.conf.

 -- Icosa Consulting <build@icosa.consulting>  Fri, 01 May 2026 18:00:00 -0600

mactelnet-proxy (0.1.5) stable; urgency=low

  * fix(deb): drop literal #DEBHELPER# from postinst/prerm comments —
    debhelper text-substitutes the token wherever it appears, including
    inside comments, expanding into stray shell that broke `dpkg -i`
    on 0.1.4 with a syntax error near `)`. Comments now reference
    "DEBHELPER" without the surrounding hashes; the actual token at
    the substitution point is preserved.
  * add optional systemd drop-in example for running the proxy inside
    a Linux VRF via `ip vrf exec ${VRF}` — shipped at
    /usr/share/doc/mactelnet-proxy/examples/vrf.conf. Includes the
    CAP_NET_ADMIN/CAP_SYS_ADMIN grants and SystemCallFilter relaxation
    that ip(8)'s bpf/cgroup setup requires.

 -- Icosa Consulting <build@icosa.consulting>  Fri, 01 May 2026 14:00:00 -0600

mactelnet-proxy (0.1.4) stable; urgency=low

  * binary reads MACTELNET_PROXY_* env vars directly; systemd
    ExecStart and Docker ENTRYPOINT collapse to a single exec-form
    line each — the /bin/sh -c '...${VAR:+-flag}...' kludge is gone
  * env-var names prefixed MACTELNET_PROXY_ to avoid collisions
    with stray shell vars; existing /etc/default/mactelnet-proxy
    files need editing on upgrade

 -- Icosa Consulting <build@icosa.consulting>  Thu, 01 May 2026 12:00:00 -0600

mactelnet-proxy (0.1.3) stable; urgency=low

  * env-var driven systemd unit (LISTEN, KEYS_DIR, MNDP_IFACE,
    AUTH_TIMEOUT, DATA_TIMEOUT, DEBUG); EnvironmentFile under
    /etc/default/ and /etc/sysconfig/ both honored
  * IP header now byte-identical to RouterOS /tool mac-telnet
    (TOS=0x00, no DF flag) — closes the only remaining wire-level
    delta from the trusted reference flow

